10 library loan records were delivered as one batch and are validated against the numbered rules that follow. No batch breaks more than one rule, and a broken rule is broken once. Judge the batch by the listed rules alone, reading each one literally; anything they do not mention is acceptable.

Fields per record: loan_id (text), desk (text), deposit (whole number), copy (text), slip_no (whole number), member (text), card (text), days_late (whole number), fine (whole number), daily_fee (whole number), branch (text), item_type (text), kiosk (text), condition_out (text), reserve_code (text), renewal_of (text), reserved (text).

Integrity rules:
R1. Every value of `branch` must be an entry of the reference list `branches` that is marked "active".
R2. For a record with `item_type` = "book", `deposit` lies between 6 and 30; for a record with `item_type` = "media", between 2 and 9 (limits included in both cases).
R3. Whenever `reserved` is "yes", `reserve_code` must be filled in.
R4. `loan_id` is the record key: a value may occur only once in the batch.
R5. No two records agree in both `card` and `copy`; agreeing in just one of the two is fine.
R6. The values of `slip_no` are consecutive in batch order: no number is skipped or repeated, wherever the count starts.
R7. A `member` that is not a key of the reference list `members` is not allowed.
R8. A filled-in `renewal_of` names the `loan_id` of another record of this batch, and that record comes before the one that names it.
R9. No value of `condition_out` other than "worn", "good", "damaged", "repaired" is accepted.

Reference list `branches` with 7 entries (key: status): BR-21: active; BR-23: active; BR-26: active; BR-53: inactive; BR-58: inactive; BR-72: active; BR-92: active

Reference list `members` with 10 keys: MB-1048, MB-1084, MB-1565, MB-3162, MB-3400, MB-3724, MB-4666, MB-4705, MB-6650, MB-7057

Note on statuses: a plain look-up rule (one that names no status) accepts any key of the list, with any status; a status is required only by a rule that names it.

